# Engine caches and local editor state
.godot/
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Video/audio and generated distribution packages stay outside source control.
*.[mM][pP]3
*.[mM][pP]4
*.avi
*.mov
*.wav
exports/
builds/
# Intermediates: synthesis WAVs, pose previews. Everything here is
# reproducible by re-running the script that made it.
build/

# Local credentials/configuration
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
credentials/
*.p12
*.pfx

# Git cannot ignore by size: inspect staged files before committing (>25 MB).

# Film build intermediates. The reel's evidence (coverage.json, beat_sheet.json,
# the input logs, _qc/REPORT.md) is tracked; the compositor's working clips and
# the rendered media are not - both are reproducible, and the media is already
# excluded by the *.mp4 rule above.
youtube/*/clips/
# A FILE glob, not a directory one: git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so `!` on paths inside `youtube/*/media/` never took effect.
youtube/*/media/*
# ...except the stills the evidence ledger HASHES. A reviewer has to be able to
# recompute those hashes from the repository, and a rendered beat video is not
# the same thing as the evidence it shows. One `!` line per hashed still.
#
# A5's five evidence cards, 1.6 MB in all. Each is a 3840 x 2160 composite of
# an engine capture and the recorded report that goes with it, written by
# scripts/compose_lost_evidence.py; re-run that script (after
# scripts/compose_a5_extras.py) and the same bytes come back.
!youtube/*/media/B03A.png
!youtube/*/media/B07.png
!youtube/*/media/B09.png
!youtube/*/media/B11.png
!youtube/*/media/B11B.png
youtube/*/mp3/*.mp3
# Lossless frame sequences from Movie Maker: 165 MB for two short takes, and
# reproducible by `scripts/render_takes.py`.
youtube/*/capture/take-*/

# The ENCODED capture is a different matter and is tracked. The *.mp4 rule
# above was written for 4K masters; take-w.mp4 is 342 KB, and the evidence
# ledger hashes it as the result half of two code-then-result pairs. With it
# excluded, a reviewer who cloned the tag got
# `Missing or escaping source: capture/take-w.mp4` from the course checker
# and could not verify anything. Found 2026-10-28 by cloning a5 into an empty
# directory and running the checker there.
!youtube/*/capture/take-w.mp4

# scripts/frame_footage_beats.py computes the two gameplay cards' numbers
# from this at build time, and the `logs/` rule below was hiding it. Git does
# not descend into an excluded directory, so the directory is un-excluded
# first and then the one file inside it.
!youtube/*/capture/logs/
!youtube/*/capture/logs/take-w-inputs.jsonl

# Machine-local build state: rewritten on every `./art final`, full of absolute
# paths, and it names the export under its pre-rename slug. Its one durable
# fact — the master's SHA-256 — is recorded deliberately in
# youtube/*/SOURCES.md instead, so it lives in exactly one place.
youtube/*/build-state.json

# Blender's own save-versions. Blender writes <name>.blend1 beside a file
# every time it re-saves it, so these appear as soon as an asset is rebuilt.
# Assignment 3 says to exclude them, and they are regenerated anyway.
*.blend1
*.blend2

# Test wrapper output. Churns on every run; the logs that are CITED are
# copied into evidence/ deliberately, which is what a reviewer should read.
logs/

# A5's film. The 4K PNG sequence and the encoded capture stay out by the rules
# above; this one still is tracked because TEST-REPORT.md cites it.
!captures/a5/warning-ramp-contact-sheet.png

# Python bytecode caches.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Re-stated AFTER the `logs/` rule above, which would otherwise win: a later
# pattern beats an earlier one, and the directory has to be un-excluded
# before git will look inside it.
!youtube/*/capture/logs/
!youtube/*/capture/logs/take-w-inputs.jsonl
